The files beside this one are 86Box's Voodoo Graphics / Voodoo 2 emulation,
copied verbatim (no edits: the port lives in ../shim and ../qemu) from

  https://github.com/86Box/86Box
  commit b0e0b7f04537b14d4149e546bd17772007831baf  (2026-09-11)
  src/video/vid_voodoo*.c  ->  vid_voodoo*.c
  src/include/86box/vid_voodoo*.h  ->  vid_voodoo*.h

Not copied: vid_voodoo_banshee.c, vid_voodoo_banshee_blitter.c (the Banshee /
Voodoo 3 are 2D+3D cards with their own VGA core; the four entry points the
Voodoo 1/2 files still call on them are stubbed in ../qemu/voodoo_shim.c and
are unreachable for type < VOODOO_BANSHEE) and vid_voodoo_codegen_x86.h (the
32-bit x86 recompiler; every 2ksbox host is 64-bit).

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (86Box's; the files carry the authors' headers --
Sarah Walker's PCem is the origin). Same licence as QEMU, so the same as
everything else this device links into.

To refresh against a newer upstream commit, run scripts/sync-86box-voodoo.sh
<commit>: it fetches those files at that commit into this directory and
prints the diff, then update the commit and date above.
